   "prompt": "Create a graph of the curve defined by the function $r=4+4\\;\\cos \\theta .$",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "solution": "<img src=\"/media/ch11/CNX_Calc_Figure_11_03_006.jpg\" alt=\"The graph of r = 4 + 4 cosθ is given. It vaguely looks look a heart tipped on its side with a rounded bottom instead of a pointed one. Specifically, the graph starts at the origin, moves into the second quadrant and increases to a rounded circle-like figure. The graph is symmetric about the x axis, so it continues its rounded circle-like figure, goes into the third quadrant, and comes to a point at the origin.\">\n<p>The name of this shape is a cardioid, which we will study further later in this section.</p>",
    "hint": "Follow the problem-solving strategy for creating a graph in polar coordinates."
   }
